# C-420: variable reference
#
# Claude Code does NOT read .env files. This file only documents the variables
# C-420 uses and where each one actually has to live.
#
# 1) NON-SECRET values: settings.json "env" block.
#    setup.sh fills these in for you. Claude Code exports them to every session,
#    tool call, and hook.
#
#    C420_HOME=C:/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/.claude        (where this config is installed)
#    PROJECTS_ROOT=C:/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/Projects   (where your own repos live)
#    MEMORY_SNAPSHOT_PATH=C:/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/.claude/memory/last_session.md
#    C420_CONTEXT_WINDOW=200000                      (1000000 for 1M-context models)
#    STATUSLINE_NAME=Your Name
#    STATUSLINE_EMAIL=you@your-domain.com
#
#    Optional, add them to the same block if a skill you use needs them:
#    CLIENT_PROJECTS_ROOT=C:/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/Client Projects   (schwifty-design)
#    DESKTOP_DIR=C:/Users/YOUR_USERNAME/Desktop                     (wp-elementor-mcp-connect)
#    CLAUDE_MEMORY_STORE_PATH=~/.claude-memory-store/projects/<encoded-cwd>/memory
#    C420_HANDOFF_DIR=<defaults to the memory folder + /handoffs>
#
#    Do NOT name anything CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. That is a built-in Claude Code
#    variable that relocates the entire config directory.
#
# 2) SECRETS: your OS environment, never settings.json or any tracked file.
#    Windows:     setx TWENTYFIRST_API_KEY "your_key"   (then restart the terminal)
#    macOS/Linux: export TWENTYFIRST_API_KEY="your_key" in ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc
#
#    TWENTYFIRST_API_KEY      used by mcp-servers/21st-magic-wrapper.cmd
#    SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN    used by mcp-servers/supabase-mcp-wrapper.cmd
#
# 3) settings.json mcpServers.context-mode has a literal placeholder path,
#    <PATH_TO_YOUR_CONTEXT_MODE_CLI>. Edit it in place, or delete that block if
#    you don't use context-mode.
